    "result_text": "Tests green. I agreed with all three findings and addressed them:\n\n**1 & 2 \u2014 orphaned `isHouseholdInUse`.** Correct. Once the household-duplicate 409 block was removed, this method had no callers anywhere (grep confirmed only the declaration + definition). I removed it from both `ClinicService` (interface + its now-misleading Javadoc) and `ClinicServiceImpl` (impl + `@Transactional` wiring). `normalizeHouseholdValue` and `householdIdFor` stay, since they're still used for the household-derived fields.\n\n**3 \u2014 stale `Sha256Hex` class doc.** Correct. Broadened the class summary to cover both the truncated upper-case `upperHexPrefix` and the full lower-case `lowerHex`.\n\nI also tidied one knock-on: `normalizeHouseholdValue`'s Javadoc said \"for duplicate comparison\" \u2014 true only while `isHouseholdInUse` existed \u2014 so I repointed it at the `householdIdFor` hash, its sole remaining caller.\n\n```\nTests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```",
